  "notes": [
    "J1443+1453: the paper reports the closest Sgr dSph encounter as 2.42 kpc from the core (T:p1-b4, T:p4-b15, T:p5-b0) but later states that it was 0.97 kpc away at 3σ confidence (T:p5-b2). This inconsistency does not change the retained HVS-candidate classification.",
    "J1443+1453: Table 1 does not explicitly state units for the J2000 RA and Dec; they are recorded in their standard sexagesimal notation with RA in hours and Dec in degrees. T:p2-b7 also reports a Galactic rest-frame radial velocity of about 228.22 ± 1.97 km/s, but this is not recorded under radial_velocity because the requested quantity is the heliocentric or barycentric line-of-sight velocity; only the heliocentric HRV is retained."
